course: dictionary
lesson: 11658
title: Ascent: climbing up
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An ascent is a climb up a mountain, a hill or stairs. It can also be an upward slope or path, or a rise to a higher place or level. «The climbers began their ascent of the mountain at dawn.» The words climbers and mountain are clues: they are going up.
explain: «The balloon's slow ascent carried it above the clouds.» Ask yourself: what is going up? The balloon is rising higher and higher, so ascent must mean the upward movement. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Ascent can also mean a rise to a higher position. «Her ascent to team captain took only one year.» Here nobody is climbing a hill: she moved up to a higher role. The opposite of ascent is descent, which means going down.
fact: An ascent is a climb up, an upward slope or path, or a rise to a higher level.
fact: The verb form is «ascend», which means to go up.
fact: Descent is the opposite of ascent: it means going down.
fact: In maths, an ascent can be the height gained, found by subtracting the lower height from the higher one.
fact: In science, a balloon's or a rocket's ascent is its journey upwards.
exercise: «The climbers rested halfway through the ascent.» What does ascent mean? | A fall down a cliff | *A climb up | A run along a flat field | A swim across a lake
exercise: What is the opposite of ascent? | Rise | Climb | *Descent | Slope
exercise: A plane rises from 300 metres to 900 metres. What is its ascent? | *600 metres | 900 metres | 300 metres | 1200 metres
test: «Her ascent to team captain took only one year.» What does ascent mean here? | A new kit | A short game | *A rise to a higher position | A fall in the team
test: «The balloon's ascent was smooth and slow.» Which direction does the balloon move in its ascent? | Sideways | *Upwards | Round and round | Downwards
exam: Which word is a noun meaning a climb up a hill or stairs? | Dip | *Ascent | Descent | Drop
